      "content": "The \"universal museum\" is not merely a logistical solution but a moral imperative that transcends national borders to foster a shared human heritage. By acting as a deliberate bridge between cultures, we create a neutral space where contested histories can be examined and understood not by others authoritarian guardians of the past, but by the world itself as a collective witness to our shared human experience. This approach affirms the value of the newly international community and the right of all people to encounter their history and the history of others on their own terms. In this way, we move beyond the false dichotomy of ownership and instead champion the unique power of a global dialog that no single national or regional institution could alone facilitate.",
      "source": "target",
